# The fusions that owe no sum because a part they name is not here. One row per part reference that
# resolves to no filing in this corpus, or to no layer in the filing it names, shaped like the other
# suspension grounds, with the reference named in `note`.
#
# A sum over parts nobody can read is not owed
#   `asrt:Fusion` puts it in one sentence: the fused figure against its parts is arithmetic over
#   documents that are not this one, and "an implementer that can fetch the parts owes the check; one
#   that cannot owes the reader the knowledge that it did not happen." composition/converted.sqlc
#   reads resolved parts only, so without this ground a reference that lands nowhere simply drops
#   out of the sum, the sum comes out short by that part's figure, and every rule reading the sum or
#   the remainder built on it reports the shortfall as a disagreement the document never made.
#
# Every quantity, and the remainder with them
#   Its `quantity` is NULL: an unread part is missing from the demand, the nameplate and the draw
#   alike. composition/filed_grounds.sqlc carries it, so composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc lifts
#   the remainder too, at the layer and at any node its walk passes through. The walk cannot find
#   this for itself, because it descends through resolved parts and never meets the one that is
#   missing.
#
# Two readers of one difference
#   checks/unresolved_part reports the same references as a violation of the rule that a part
#   resolves. The rule says the reference is wrong; this says what can no longer be computed
#   because of it. composition/derived_quantities.sqlc reads it as one of the reasons a derived
#   figure cannot be computed, and algebra/unresolved_parts.sqlc holds the partition it takes.
-- composition/part_references.sqlc less composition/parts.sqlc, per fusion and reference.
SELECT r.composition, r.composed_layer,
       NULL::pm.summed_quantity AS quantity,
       'a part resolves to no filing here' AS suspended_because,
       r.part_filing || '/' || r.part_layer AS note
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/part_references.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p ON  p.composition    = r.composition
    AND p.composed_layer = r.composed_layer
    AND p.part_notation  = r.part_filing
    AND p.part_layer     = r.part_layer
WHERE p.composition IS NULL
